{
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "c03-title-01",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter three. The sign of naṣb: fatha.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-02",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It works just like damma and kasra. With al, or when owned, it takes one vowel. Otherwise, it takes tanween.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-01",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First card. With al, or when the word is owned, it takes one fatha only. No tanween.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "sign:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-02",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "With al, like the lesson.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-03",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الدَّرْسَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-04",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Or owned, like the teacher's book.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-05",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابَ المُدَرِّسِ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-06",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Book is owned, so it takes one fatha.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-07",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Second card. No al. Fatha with tanween, written with an extra alif.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "sign:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-08",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابًا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-09",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "صَبَاحًا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-10",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Third card. The exception.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "sign:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-11",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Some words end in a round ta, or in alif and hamza. They still take fatha with tanween. But there is no extra alif.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-12",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "رَغْبَةً",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-signs-13",
   "scene": "c03-signs",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَسَاءً",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-01",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter four. Colour key: the new jobs.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-02",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A big box is the word's job in the sentence. A small box is a word with its own rule.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-01",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Navy is the verb. The action. Past and order verbs are fixed.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "key:verb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-02",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Orange is the doer. Who did the action? It takes rafʿ, with damma.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "key:doer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-03",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The four new jobs all take naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-04",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Pink is the object. What? Whom? The thing the action falls on.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "key:obj"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-05",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Teal is the purpose. Why? The reason for the action.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "key:purp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-06",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Brown is time or place. When? Where? With no preposition.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "key:when"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-07",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Olive is the state. How? The state of the doer or object.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "key:state"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-key-08",
   "scene": "c04-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The small boxes from last lesson still work. After a preposition. Ownership. Adjective. And after wa.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "old"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-01",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter five. The four naṣb jobs at a glance.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-02",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Find the verb and the doer. For every other noun, ask the question. The one it answers is its job.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-01",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Object. What? Whom? The thing the action falls on. The student wrote the lesson.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:obj"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-02",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ الدَّرْسَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-03",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Purpose. Why? The reason. Usually an action noun with tanween. The student stood up out of respect.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:purp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-04",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "وَقَفَ الطَّالِبُ احْتِرَامًا",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-05",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Time or place. When? Where? No preposition. Zayd travelled in the morning.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:when"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-06",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "سَافَرَ زَيْدٌ صَبَاحًا",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-07",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "State. How? The state of the doer or object, with no al. Zayd came hurrying.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:state"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-glance-08",
   "scene": "c05-glance",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ زَيْدٌ مُسْرِعًا",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": []
  }
 ]
}